samples.evidence:
The delta cements (and now tests) that `resolveAnchoredLocalCursor().cursor` carries `lineAffinity` across an upstream edit. Its single production consumer is `docs-view.tsx:368 editor.restoreLocalCursor(resolvedLocalCursor.cursor, ...)`, which lands in `packages/docs/src/view/editor.ts:3592-3598`:
```
restoreLocalCursor: (cursorPos, range) => {
  if (cursorPos && doc.findBlock(cursorPos.blockId)) {
    const block = doc.getBlock(cursorPos.blockId);
    cursor.moveTo({ blockId: cursorPos.blockId, offset: Math.min(...) });
```
`Cursor.moveTo` defaults `affinity` to `'backward'` (packages/docs/src/view/cursor.ts:28-31) and unconditionally overwrites `this.lineAffinity`. So after every remote change the local caret's affinity is reset to `'backward'`, while `publishResolvedLocalCursor` (docs-view.tsx:375) simultaneously broadcasts the preserved `'forward'` affinity — the local render and presence disagree, and a caret sitting on a wrap boundary visibly jumps to the end of the previous line whenever a peer edits. Fix belongs on `restoreLocalCursor`: pass `cursorPos.lineAffinity` through to `moveTo`.

